answer.summary:
Promote Aurora 500ml PET and take price on Aurora 1.5L and 6x330ml multipack; avoid pricing or promo changes on the can.

Under the candidate plan (scenario index 1), Aurora weekly gross profit rises versus baseline (0.focal.gp.value to 1.focal.gp.value) while also lifting volume (0.focal.volume.value to 1.focal.volume.value). This improvement is driven by higher 1.5L and multipack pricing and the added 500ml PET promotion (1.focal_bridge.price, 1.focal_bridge.promo, 1.focal_bridge.total), under assumptions A-003, A-004, A-005, A-006, A-007, A-008, A-009, A-012, A-013, A-014a, A-014b, A-014c, A-014d, A-015, A-016, A-017, A-017b, A-018, A-019, A-020, A-021, A-022, A-023.

The cross-check scenario (index 3), which only takes price on 1.5L and multipack without extra 500ml PET promo, yields less Aurora gross profit uplift than the full candidate plan (1.focal.gp.value vs 3.focal.gp.value), though still above baseline (0.focal.gp.value to 3.focal.gp.value). Its gain comes mainly from price on the larger, less-elastic packs with neutral promo (3.focal_bridge.price, 3.focal_bridge.promo, 3.focal_bridge.total) under assumptions A-003, A-004, A-005, A-006, A-013, A-014a, A-014b, A-014c, A-014d, A-015, A-016, A-017, A-017b, A-018, A-019, A-020, A-021, A-022, A-023.

Downside input-cost stress (index 4) shows a lower Aurora gross profit than the baseline (0.focal.gp.value to 4.focal.gp.value), driven purely by higher costs (4.focal_bridge.cogs, 4.focal_bridge.total) without any pricing or promo offset, under assumptions A-013, A-014a, A-014b, A-014c, A-014d, A-015, A-016, A-018, A-019, A-020, A-021, A-022, A-023.

The “Likely loser – take price on elastic can, promote low-margin multipack” scenario (index 2) was refused due to lack of local support for the requested Aurora-multipack_6x330ml price/promo combination and so cannot be used for decision-making.

Net impact by Aurora pack in the candidate scenario vs baseline: Aurora 500ml PET volume and gross profit both increase (0.volume.Aurora-pet_500ml.value to 1.volume.Aurora-pet_500ml.value; 0.gp.Aurora-pet_500ml.value to 1.gp.Aurora-pet_500ml.value), largely due to the new promotion and favourable cross-pack shifts (1.bridge.Aurora-pet_500ml.promo_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-pet_500ml.cross_pack_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-pet_500ml.total_cents). Aurora 1.5L and 6x330ml multipack show gross profit gains despite modest volume softness (0.volume.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.value to 1.volume.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.value; 0.gp.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.value to 1.gp.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.value; 0.volume.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.value to 1.volume.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.value; 0.gp.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.value to 1.gp.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.value), thanks to higher net price and supportive cross-pack effects (1.bridge.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.price_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.cross_pack_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-bottle_1500ml.total_cents; 1.bridge.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.price_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.cross_pack_cents, 1.bridge.Aurora-multipack_6x330ml.total_cents). Aurora can remains broadly stable in volume and gross profit vs baseline (0.volume.Aurora-can_330ml.value to 1.volume.Aurora-can_330ml.value; 0.gp.Aurora-can_330ml.value to 1.gp.Aurora-can_330ml.value), indicating no need for additional price or promo leverage there in the recommended plan.

Overall, among supported scenarios ranked on Aurora gross profit (evaluation_tool_call_id=call_0005, ranking entries index=1,3,0,4), the candidate plan (index 1) is the strongest, followed by the cross-check (index 3), then baseline (index 0), with the downside cost stress case (index 4) worst.

